WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.762 --> 00:00:02.904
- [Voiceover] At the end of World War II,

00:00:02.904 --> 00:00:05.987
the Soviets were holding
Berlin under siege.

00:00:05.987 --> 00:00:08.905
In order to save millions
of people from starvation,

00:00:08.905 --> 00:00:13.348
the US and Allies devised
a plan to airlift in food.

00:00:13.348 --> 00:00:16.977
One American pilot decided
to take it a step further.

00:00:16.977 --> 00:00:19.095
He delivered candy.

00:00:19.095 --> 00:00:21.569
- My name is Gail Halvorsen,

00:00:21.569 --> 00:00:25.521
but I'm known as the Berlin Candy Bomber.

00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:28.304
I didn't think that the
airlift would last very long,

00:00:28.304 --> 00:00:31.817
so I thought, I'd better get
a movie in, of this operation

00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:34.017
before they send me home.

00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:34.850
- [Voiceover] One day,

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.002
while filming the planes
taking off and landing,

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:37.956
Gail became aware

00:00:37.956 --> 00:00:40.695
that there were some young
children watching him.

00:00:40.695 --> 00:00:43.522
He went over to talk to
them, and after a while,

00:00:43.522 --> 00:00:44.689
he realized...

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:49.183
- “Dummy, don't you know
kids like chocolate?”

00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:51.675
And I knew that they had not had chocolate

00:00:51.675 --> 00:00:54.362
in the stores in Berlin for two years.

00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:55.739
And I reached in my pocket,

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.345
and all I had was two sticks
of Wrigley's Doublemint gum.

00:01:00.345 --> 00:01:03.017
I broke the two sticks in
half, gave it to the kids.

00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:04.465
And the kids with half a stick

00:01:04.465 --> 00:01:06.794
tore off the wrapper into thin strips

00:01:06.794 --> 00:01:09.248
and passed it to those without gum.

00:01:09.248 --> 00:01:13.471
Those who had received the
wrappers put it at their nose

00:01:13.471 --> 00:01:16.054
and smelled a piece of wrapper.

00:01:17.032 --> 00:01:19.008
- [Voiceover] Inspired
by their generosity,

00:01:19.008 --> 00:01:20.704
he decided that next flight,

00:01:20.704 --> 00:01:22.568
he would drop them chocolate and candy

00:01:22.568 --> 00:01:24.504
via parachute from the plane.

00:01:24.504 --> 00:01:25.337
- [Gail] They said,

00:01:25.337 --> 00:01:27.102
"How do we know what airplane you're in?"

00:01:27.102 --> 00:01:29.255
And so I said, “When I
come over the airfield,

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.470
I'll wiggle the wings
of that big airplane.”

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.151
They said, "Oh, great."

00:01:33.151 --> 00:01:34.752
- [Voiceover] True to
his word, the next day

00:01:34.752 --> 00:01:37.627
Gail began to drop the packages.

00:01:37.627 --> 00:01:39.687
What started with just two sticks of gum

00:01:39.687 --> 00:01:43.354
eventually turned into
23 tons of chocolate.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:47.366
- From then on, I was known in the press

00:01:47.366 --> 00:01:50.350
and all the kids in Berlin,
“that's Uncle Wiggly Wings.”

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:51.422
- [Voiceover] And in case you wondering

00:01:51.422 --> 00:01:54.300
if the Candy Bomber still
has a sweet tooth...

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.558
- Oh, yeah, I still eat chocolate.

00:01:56.558 --> 00:01:58.836
I like dark chocolate.

00:01:58.836 --> 00:02:01.503
(upbeat music)

